--TEST--
an enum, its cases and a `type` alias are three kinds a regex cannot tell apart from any other identifier, which is why the parse answers them, `rule:ide/semantic-tokens-carry-the-qualifiers`, `rule:types/declaration`
--FILE--
<?nvs
type Id = uint;
enum Status: int {
    case Draft = 1;
    case Live = 2;
}
--REQUEST--
semanticTokens
--EXPECT--
2:6+2 type
3:6+6 enum
4:10+5 enumMember
5:10+4 enumMember
